course: dictionary
lesson: 9136
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and snap is a good example. «The stick snapped in two.» The clues are stick and in two, so snap here means break suddenly with a sharp crack.
explain: «Zane snaps, "It's Mum's house."» Here snap means say something quickly and angrily. Check by swapping in a meaning: "Zane breaks, It's Mum's house" makes no sense, so snap must mean something else.
explain: Look at the words next to snap. A cold snap is sudden cold weather, and a snap decision is one made very quickly. The words beside snap tell you which meaning to use.
fact: Snap can be a verb, a noun or an adjective. As a verb it changes: snap, snaps, snapped, snapping.
fact: «Snap» means to break suddenly with a sharp cracking sound.
fact: «Snap» can mean to say something quickly and angrily, or to bite quickly, as an animal does.
fact: «Snap» can also mean a photograph (informal, British), or a card game where you shout "Snap!" when two cards match.
exercise: «The dry twig snapped under my foot.» What does snapped mean? | Smiled widely | Went soft and bendy | *Broke suddenly with a sharp crack | Shouted for help
exercise: «Zane snaps, "It's Mum's house."» What does snaps mean here? | Takes a photograph | Clicks his fingers | Breaks in two | *Says something quickly and angrily
exercise: Nadia says, "Let's make a snap decision." What does snap mean here? | A photograph | Very slowly and carefully | Something that breaks | *Quick, made without long thinking
test: «The alligator snapping turtle snaps its jaws shut.» What does snaps mean here? | Says something quickly | Clicks its fingers | *Bites quickly, closing its jaws fast | Takes a photograph
test: "It was a cold snap, so we wore our coats." What does cold snap mean? | A photo of the cold | A cold drink | *Sudden cold weather | A sudden card game
exam: In the card game, you shout "Snap!" when what happens? | The deck is empty | You lose your turn | *Two cards match | Someone sneezes
